I am also trying to estimate a growth mixture model in Stan, but I am not sure if I am doing it correctly. I have read the mixture model chapter from the manual. If I am doing it correctly, than I am almost surely doing it poorly. So far the model compiles and begins sampling, but on my machine it has taken about 6 hours to get to 10% of 2000 iterations [Warmup] for Chain 1. In a previous attempt to let the model run overnight, just a single chain, 200 iterations, the effective sample size for k(# of components) was very small relative to the other parameters, but I don't remember the specifics before my computer froze.

